# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# A std::exception_ptr stored in a future is reference-counted with atomics
# inside libstdc++/libsupc++, which distributions ship *without* TSan
# instrumentation. When the caller's thread reads e.what() and a worker later
# drops the last reference and frees the exception, TSan cannot see the atomic
# refcount that orders the two and reports a false data race inside the
# exception's destructor. Only the destruction of standard exception objects is
# suppressed; races in the pool or the tests themselves are still reported.
race:std::runtime_error::~runtime_error
race:std::logic_error::~logic_error
